----------------------------------------------------------------\
6. COMMON EDITS YOU CAN DO YOURSELF\
----------------------------------------------------------------\
Open the .html file in a text editor (VS Code recommended \'97 free,\
and it color-codes the HTML so it's easy to read).\
\
- Change text: find the words, type over them. Save. Refresh browser.\
- Add a news item: in news.html, copy an existing <div class="item">\
  ... </div> line and edit its date/text.\
- Add a publication: in publications.html, copy an existing\
  <article class="pub"> ... </article> block and edit it.\
- Swap a photo: replace the file in members/ or photos/ with a new\
  one of the SAME name. (Or change the name in the code to match.)\
- Add a gallery event: copy a <div class="shot" ...></div> line in\
  photos.html, set its data-base/count/ext/caption/year, and add the\
  matching image files to the photos/ folder.\
\
TIP: After editing, do a "hard refresh" in the browser to avoid\
seeing a cached old version:\
  Mac Safari:  Cmd + Option + R\
  Mac Chrome:  Cmd + Shift + R\
  Or open the file in a private/incognito window.\
\
